  reason: "The seed trampoline decides whether a gunbc run may proceed unwrapped BEFORE the corpus is resolved, so it cannot evaluate gunbc.compute.unit_bounds user_work_scope_standing and mirrors its arms. The revision job's guest unit runs in an unmodeled system.slice under its own MemoryMax= and MemorySwapMax=0; the fold admits it only on the ONE check -- a live finite enclosing memory.max observed on the process's own cgroup chain (gunbc.compute.unit_bounds live_enclosing_bound, reading through extdeps.linux.cgroup_v2_memory) -- and no exempt premise discharges itself any more: not the CI environment, not a runner-slot path, not a slice or unit path. These items are that check's mirror: the premise classifier, the chain walk over /sys/fs/cgroup, its typed causes (unread / no finite max / zero / swap still allowed), the located line naming the cgroup consulted, the fall-through wire the trampoline prints, and the fixture-tree tests that execute it (including the RED pairs whose cgroup memory.max reads max). The mirror is held to the .dag arms by test.claim.live_deploy.user_work_slice_witness the_seed_trampoline_mirrors_the_declared_wrap_standing.",
